    "result_text": "Build succeeds and the acceptance test passes. The audit log confirms the new format live: `customerCode=NSW-16E6609E`.\n\n## Summary\n\nRedesigned owner identity from the old `<CITY3>-<LAST3>-<NNNN>` sequence-based code to `<REGION>-<HASH8>`. Since the customer code is written in exactly one place and every downstream value derives from it, the change stayed small and localized.\n\n**`CustomerCode.java`** \u2014 Now the single definition of `<REGION>-<HASH8>`:\n- `format(region, telephone, lastName)` builds the code, with a private `hash8` computing the first 8 upper-case hex chars of SHA-256 over `telephone + lastName`.\n- New `region(customerCode)` parses the region segment back out, so consumers read the identity rather than recomputing.\n- Made `public` so the mapper can read the region; sequence/prefix logic removed.\n\n**`AssignOwnerCustomerCode.java`** \u2014 Derives the region via the existing `Locality.region(city, postcode)` and hashes the already-normalized telephone + last name. No longer needs the repository or per-city counting.\n\n**`OwnerMapper.locality`** \u2014 Moved onto the new identity: reads the region segment from `customerCode` (falling back to postcode/city derivation only when the code is absent, e.g. unsaved/seed rows).\n\n**Automatic (no code change needed):** `membershipNumber` (`<customerCode>-M<YY>`), `checkDigit` (Luhn over the code's digits), and the create audit record all already read `customerCode`, so they now reflect the region-and-hash identity.\n\n**Not touched:** `SameCity` stays \u2014 it's still used by `EnsureCityHasCapacity` for the per-city capacity rule; only the sequence use was dropped.\n\n**Docs:** Updated the `customerCode`, `membershipNumber`, and `locality` descriptions/examples in `openapi.yml` for consistency.\n\nThe new code fits `customer_code VARCHAR(20)` comfortably (`UNKNOWN-XXXXXXXX` = 16 chars).",
